 :decision
 {:smallest-defensible-boundary "One fixed Python stdlib OS-edge driver with three roles: nonblocking supervisor, single network worker, single durable-store writer. Use an independently allocated agent-owned cgroup v2 subtree for the aggregate cap, not the existing unit. No installed service/daemon and no generic process runner. Keep NBB for existing portable laws, offline artifact preparation and later offline scoring; never launch Node/NBB as an uncounted member of the live client."
  :why-three "A supervisor performing fsync can itself stall and miss its timer. The network worker must not perform store IO, and may POST only after a durable writer acknowledgement. Writer OOM/stall must not kill the watchdog. A two-role design with synchronous supervisor store writes fails the hard-watchdog requirement."
  :as-only-alternative "32MiB supervisor + 48MiB writer + 128MiB worker hard RLIMIT_AS = 208MiB aggregate user address space, if all helpers are included and no threads/forks occur. This bounds mapped user RSS conservatively for these reviewed processes, but NOT aggregate cgroup-charged memory: socket buffers, kernel allocations and filesystem page cache are outside AS. RLIMIT_RSS is not the Linux answer. Therefore AS-only is NOT accepted as an unqualified aggregate-client-256MiB guarantee."
  :concrete-memory-fix "Qualify one narrowly owned ephemeral cgroup allocation (possibly an agent-owned transient USER scope with Delegate=yes, MemoryMax=268435456, MemorySwapMax=0, TasksMax=3), without installing a service or modifying OCR/i3 units. Parent must first review exact scope allocation/cleanup authority. Do not infer blanket systemd-run authority from its presence. If unavailable, remain blocked; do not quietly reinterpret 256MiB as heap/RSS sampling."
  :remaining-logical-limits "A normal Linux userspace watchdog is not a hard real-time proof. SIGKILL cannot guarantee death at exactly 30s for a task stuck in uninterruptible kernel IO; pending filesystem IO can complete after kill. Nor does closing a socket cancel already accepted inference in the existing ThreadingHTTPServer. Literal universal guarantees of durable final evidence, no filesystem mutation after 30s, and server cancellation within 30s cannot be supplied by this design or by cgroup.kill. Preserve these explicit holds rather than authorize execution by redefining them."}

